# The assessment of MODEL-ROUTE-015 against this build. The requirement identifier is
# this file's stem and appears nowhere inside it, because a second place to spell the
# identity is a second place for it to be wrong -- the rule OD-SPEC-007 chose for a
# record registration, and CHK-003.assessment states for this registry.
#
# MODEL-ROUTE-015: "Every resolved effort request shall emit an EffortMappingRecord
# containing the canonical requested effort, provider-native setting or
# executor-controlled disposition, mapping quality of Exact, Approximate, Unsupported,
# or ExecutorControlled, package/version, rationale, and limitations."
#
# MappingQuality and EffortMappingRecord carry the full named shape, and the old entry's
# reason for Partial is now false twice over. It said nothing registers a model backend or
# executor implementation anywhere in this workspace, so no effort request could be
# resolved; P40-MODEL-ROUTING-DISPATCH-WIRING declares two -- an AgentExecutorPackage and a
# ModelBackendPackage, through Declared_Targets -- and an effort request really is resolved
# against them.
#
# The requirement's trigger therefore fires now and its obligation does not. DispatchConfig
# is the resolved shape: Selected_Dispatch carries the profile's canonical effort into it
# unchanged, which is decision 6's "effort is carried, never mapped", and hands it to a
# backend. No EffortMappingRecord is constructed at that point or any other. Nothing
# records that Claude Code's disposition is executor-controlled while Ollama's is opaque --
# a distinction Declared_Targets now states as ModelSelection and MappingQuality has a
# variant for -- and nothing names the package version either declaration carries.
verdict: Partial
site: crates/packages/nomos-model-package/src/effort_mapping_record.rs#EffortMappingRecord
gap: crates/orchestration/nomos-agent-orchestration/src/dispatch_config.rs#DispatchConfig
